  "notes": "Asked for before enabling the unrolled recursive grammar. The 248,320-entry vocabulary is swept once per new automaton state, so the cost is (misses) x (sweep) and is flat in total grammar size: 1,737 states at depth 1 already costs 2,720 ms per token, and 9,483 states costs 2,820. JSON-shaped GBNF sweeps cost ~3.5 s each because their string/whitespace classes accept nearly every byte; the schema automaton rejects most tokens on the first character and sweeps in ~250 ms.",
